      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "1b8d6dbb-c29a-5b1e-90cf-19263619fc29",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Michael Douglas\n- Songs: “Man on the Edge”, “Running Free”, “Out of the Silent Planet”, “Total Eclipse”, “Mission From 'Arry”, “Bayswater Ain't a Bad Place to Be”, “I Live My Way”, “Run to the Hills”, “2 Minutes to Midnight”, “Be Quick or Be Dead”\n- Albums: Best of the 'B' Sides, The Number of the Beast\n- Films: Falling Down\n- Bands: Iron Maiden\n\nFacts:\n- Michael Douglas was born on September 25, 1944, and he is an American actor and producer.\n- Iron Maiden released the single “Running Free” in 1980.\n- Iron Maiden released the single “Run to the Hills” in 1982, and its original B-side was “Total Eclipse”.\n- Iron Maiden released the single “2 Minutes to Midnight” in 1984, and its original B-side was “Mission From 'Arry”.\n- Iron Maiden released the single “Be Quick or Be Dead” in 1992, and its original B-side was “Bayswater Ain't a Bad Place to Be”.\n- Iron Maiden released the single “Man on the Edge” in 1995, and its original B-side was “I Live My Way”.\n- The Iron Maiden song “Man on the Edge” is based on the film Falling Down, which starred Michael Douglas.\n- From 1998 onward, “Total Eclipse” was added to the album The Number of the Beast.\n- Iron Maiden released the single “Out of the Silent Planet” in 2000.\n- The album Best of the 'B' Sides covers Iron Maiden singles from “Running Free” through “Out of the Silent Planet”, but it excludes several original B-sides, including “Total Eclipse”, “Mission From 'Arry”, “Bayswater Ain't a Bad Place to Be”, and “I Live My Way”.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "25c5d49a-ca44-5a98-a4e2-4b9a336aca6c",
        "text": "Page: Man on the Edge. Sentence: The song is based on the film \"Falling Down\", starring Michael Douglas.\nPage: Michael Douglas. Sentence: Michael Kirk Douglas (born September 25, 1944) is an American actor and producer.\nPage: Best of the 'B' Sides. Sentence: It covers all of their singles from their first (1980's \"Running Free\") to 2000's \"Out of the Silent Planet\", although several of the band's original B-sides were excluded from the collection: \"Total Eclipse\" (from \"Run to the Hills\", 1982, although this has been added to the album \"The Number of the Beast\" from 1998 onwards), \"Mission From 'Arry\" (from \"2 Minutes to Midnight\", 1984); \"Bayswater Ain't a Bad Place to Be\" (from \"Be Quick or Be Dead\", 1992); and \"I Live My Way\" (from \"Man on the Edge\", 1995).",
